specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:165:Requests a page of conversation summaries for the authenticated user on this connection. It is independent of a `user_message`, so the server answers it without waiting for a streaming turn. A client-supplied `userId`, including one nested in `before`, is ignored: the connection's authenticated user is the only authority for the list ([validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L48), [validated by: forwards only the two cursor fields a list_sessions frame defines](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L40)).

